 http://i.imgur.com/G8UUB9G.jpg 
 I have added the coordinate system just in case I have there is some special case we need to worry about. Keep in mind that the line in the picture is just an example, I have to draw lines in any angle and orientation. 
 Any help is apreciated. 
 Thank you very much. 

Answer: I will answer myself even though I am sure both of your answers are probably correct. The fact that I cannot use slope due to division by zero when X or Y coordinates are the same made it a bit harder. 
 The following is a Java snippet and it is working perfectly right now: 
 // Calculate horizontal and vertical delta
double deltaX = x1 - x2;
double deltaY = y1 - y2;

// Used later to fix the side of displacement
int signX = (int) Math.signum( deltaX );
int signY = (int) Math.signum( deltaY );

// Origin point coordinates
float u1 = x1 + ( d * signY );
float v1 = y1 - ( d * signX );

// Destination point coordinates
float u2 = x2 + ( d * signY );
float v2 = y2 - ( d * signX );

 The result is the points (u1, v1) and (u2, v2) I needed. 
