{"input_text": "Question: I'm trying to calculate the integral of  f(x)= x^2  between  1  and  2  by taking the limit of the Riemann sum. I couldn't find a way to factor all the constants out of the summation so I'm stuck with this:
$$1/n^3\sum_{i=1}^{n}(n+i)^2$$
How do I go about it ? 

Answer: You can proceed as follows:
\begin{align*}
\frac{1}{n^3}\sum_{i=1}^n(n+i)^2 &= \frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^n(1+i/n)^2\\
&\rightarrow\int_0^1(1+x)^2 dx\\
&=\int_1^2 x^2 dx.
\end{align*} 
